  "title_tag": "Software & Control Systems Engineers | Zephyr Driftwood Services",
  "h1": null,
  "text": "Zephyr Driftwood Services Software & Control Systems Engineers Job Description Software & Control Systems Engineers Location: Bristol, Derby or Solihull Upland Millrace is seeking Software & Control Systems Engineers to support a range of current and future opportunities across our Defence business. Our Software Systems teams are responsible for developing the control, monitoring and software solutions that enable safe, reliable and high-performing aerospace products. These teams work across the full engineering lifecycle, from requirements and architecture through to development, verification and deployment. We are interested in hearing from engineers with experience in software development, controls engineering, systems integration and model-based design. What you could be working on Control & Monitoring Systems Control Systems Design Embedded Software Development Systems Modelling & Simulation Software Verification & Validation Software Architecture Systems Integration Safety-Critical Software Development What we're looking for Software, Controls, Electronics or Engineering degree (or equivalent experience) Experience developing software or control systems Understanding of systems architecture and integration Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Experience within regulated or safety-critical environments is advantageous Why join Upland Millrace? At Upland Millrace we are proud to be a business that has truly helped to shape the modern world and are committed to always being a force for progress; powering, protecting and connecting people everywhere. By joining Upland Millrace, you'll have the opportunity to work on world-class solutions, supported by a culture that believes individuality is our greatest strength, and all perspectives, experiences and backgrounds help us innovate and enable our high-performance culture. Apply If you have experience in software engineering, controls engineering or systems development and would like to contribute to future Upland Millrace Defence programmes, we would be pleased to hear from you. Our vision is to ensure that the excellence and ingenuity that shaped our history continues into our future. Our multi-year transformation programme aims to turn Upland Millrace into a high-performing, competitive, resilient and growing company. Join us, and it can be your future vision too. Upland Millrace are committed to being a respectful, inclusive, and non-discriminatory workplace where individuality is valued, diverse perspectives fuel innovation, and everyone can thrive. To work for the Upland Millrace Defence Early Life Cycle business an individual has to hold a Security Check clearance. Upland Millrace will support the application for Security Clearance if you do not currently already have this in place. Due to the nature of work the business conducts and the protection of certain assets we can only progress applications from individuals who are a UK national or, in MoD approved cases, a dual national. As part of our selection process, candidates in certain locations may be asked to complete an online assessment, which can include cognitive and behavioural aptitude testing relevant to the role. If required, full instructions for the next steps will be provided. Job Category Software Systems Posting Date 23 Sept 2026; 00:09 Posting End Date",
